   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6eCI",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I'm running because too many people in Hawke's Bay work hard and still struggle to get by. People shouldn't have to choose between paying the rent, seeing a doctor, and putting kai on the table. Cyclone Gabrielle should have been our chance to build back better – not just to restore what was there before, but to ask what kind of Hawke's Bay we want to build for the people who live here."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6eED",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I will bring energy, conviction, and knowledge of Hawke's Bay to Parliament. I've spent my spare time over the last few years campaigning on climate, housing and workers' rights. My background in meteorology and community campaigning means I understand the risks facing our region; my experience organising has taught me how to turn that understanding into real change. I'll bring that same energy and determination to fighting for you, your whānau, and the Bay. "
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6eG8",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Fight for our hospital: Quality public healthcare that everybody can access quickly and affordably."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6eI3",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Keep good jobs here: A Hawke's Bay where well-paid local workers can build the future of our region."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6eJy",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Build back better: Protect our homes, communities and growers from the changing climate."
     }
    ],
